.TH VDIR 1
.SH NAME
vdir \- visual directory browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vdir
[
.B -r
]
[
.I directory
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Vdir
browses a directory in a rio window, initially the working directory
or the directory given as an argument.
Right-click folders to navigate and files to send them to the plumber.
The Home, Open, and Up toolbar icons navigate; the two creation icons
create directories and files. Middle-click an entry to rename or delete it.
Deletion is recursive only when
.B -r
is given.
.PP
Click Terminal, choose terminal here from the middle-button menu, or press
t to open an interactive rc window in the displayed directory.
This action does not require a running plumber.
.PP
Page Up and Page Down scroll. Home goes to $home (or / if unset),
Up goes to the parent, r refreshes, Space plumbs the directory path,
and q or Delete exits.
.PP
Colors are read at startup from /dev/theme using name RRGGBB lines.
The background uses titleback when supplied, otherwise back.
Directory and executable colors default to bright blue and green.
Missing or invalid theme values retain defaults.
.SH FILES
.TF /dev/theme
.TP
.B /dev/theme
optional palette served by rio
.TP
.B /dev/wctl
creates terminal windows
.TP
.B /dev/wdir
updated to the displayed path
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/vdir
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR rio (1),
.IR rio (4),
.IR plumber (4)
